 Claude Code in a terminal, under `~/.claude`): its plugins are not listed, and installs and updates from it are refused. The sessions the app starts load plugins only from your organization's marketplaces, the organization plugins directory, the app's own uploads and the user's own skills folder, enforced through Claude Code's marketplace allowlist (`strictKnownMarketplaces`, passed as the app's managed settings). Nothing is deleted: removing the key or setting it back to `true` restores them. Marketplaces provisioned by your organization (`allowedPluginMarketplaces`) and the organization plugins directory are unaffected, and plugins users uploaded are governed by `userPluginUploadsEnabled`, not this key.\n\nThis is a feature-availability control, not a data boundary. Claude Code in a terminal reads the same `~/.claude` folder and is governed only by its own managed settings, not by this key. Claude Code may ignore this allowlist on a device that deploys its own Claude Code managed settings; restrict marketplaces in those settings as well.\n\nThis key applies only while the app runs in third-party mode. If users could otherwise sign in to Claude.ai on the device, also set `disableDeploymentModeChooser` so the app stays in third-party mode.",{docsUrl:`${cr.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/configuration#userpluginmarketplacesenabled`})}}),userPluginUploadsEnabled:se.field(wt.z.boolean().optional(),{flatKey:"userPluginUploadsEnabled",remotePolicy:{hotApplied:!0},support:{enabled:{scopes:["3p"],availableInVersion:"1.37937.0"}},title:be.msg({defaultMessage:"Allow user-added plugins",id:"FC6Rd6B6Wv"}),default:{displayOnly:!0},failClosedValue:!1,category:"sandbox",group:Tm.GENERAL_RESTRICTIONS_GROUP,order:6.7,description:{short:se.shortDescription(be.msg({defaultMessage:"Allow users to add their own plugins. When off, every in-app option for adding one is hidden and uploads that still reach the app are refused.",id:"7AFPPgSJBu"})),long:se.longDescription("When on (default), users can