file on the device still applies; when both are set, this key wins where the app's configuration is admin-managed (MDM, the admin console, or a device-managed bootstrap URL) and otherwise applies only while that file sets none. `allowedWorkspaceFolders` still applies on the remote host. Claude Code's managed settings on a host replace the sandbox, network, permission, and MCP rules this app sends unless they set `parentSettingsBehavior` to `\"merge\"`.",{docsUrl:`${zn.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/ssh-remote-sessions`})}}),sshClientPath:K.field(K.annotate(Sa.safeHelperPath.optional(),{pathKind:"file"}),{flatKey:"sshClientPath",support:{enabled:{scopes:["3p"],availableInVersion:"1.46388.1"},executionTarget:"desktop"},betaFeatureKey:"sshRemoteSessions",remotePolicy:{requiresUserConsent:!0},failClosedValue:sj.SSH_CLIENT_UNREADABLE_STAND_IN,unreadableStandIn:!0,title:B.msg({defaultMessage:"SSH client program",id:"TnZHycC4Xk"}),category:"sandbox",group:xr.CODE_SURFACE_GROUP,order:16.5,placeholder:B.msg({defaultMessage:"/opt/openssh/bin/ssh",id:"matzhaiItp"}),predicates:{show:(e)=>{var t;return((t=e.codeSurface)===null||t===void 0?void 0:t.enabled)!==!1}},description:{short:K.shortDescription(B.msg({defaultMessage:"Absolute path to the OpenSSH ssh program the app runs for SSH sessions. Unset: the first ssh on the user\u2019s PATH.",id:"CkU2BFhxiC"})),long:K.longDescription("Pins which OpenSSH client the app runs wherever it starts `ssh`: evaluating the user's SSH configuration (`ssh -G`), making the SSH connection and its channels, and the Code tab's terminal. `ssh-keygen` and `ssh-add` are taken from the same directory when they exist there, otherwise from PATH. The program must be OpenSSH 7.6 or newer (on Windows, Win32-OpenSSH 9.4 or newer to carry the connection); on macOS and Linux a wrapper script that ends in one is accepted, on Windows it must be a native `.exe` (not a .cmd, .bat or .ps1 script). When this key is set and the program is missing, cannot be run, or is too old, SSH sessions fail with an error telling the user to ask their IT administrator (the configured path is in its details) \u2014 the app never falls back to another ssh. The connection itself runs through this program on the system-OpenSSH engine, which the SSH connection engine setting's `system-openssh` value selects on every platform, including Windows; when the app's built-in SSH library makes the connection instead, this key still governs configuration evaluation (`ssh -G`), host-key lookups (`ssh-keygen`) and the terminal.",{docsUrl:`${zn.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/ssh-remote-sessions`})}}),sshTransport:K.field(Re.z.enum(["auto","system-openssh","builtin"]).optional(),{flatKey:"sshTransport",support:{enabled:{scopes:["3p"],availableInVersion:"1.52386.0"},executionTarget:"desktop"},betaFeatureKey:"sshRemoteSessions",title:B.msg({defaultMessage:"SSH connection engine",id:"SshTransportTitle"}),default:{displayOnly:"auto"},optionLabels:{auto:B.msg({defaultMessage:"Automatic (the build\u2019s default)",id:"SshTransportAuto"}),"system-openssh":B.msg({defaultMessage:"System OpenSSH client",id:"SshTransportSystemOpenSsh"}),builtin:B.msg({defaultMessage:"Built-in SSH library",id:"SshTransportBuiltin"})},category:"sandbox",group:xr.CODE_SURFACE_GROUP,order:16.7,predicates:{show:(e)=>{var t;return((t=e.codeSurface)===null||t===void 0?void 0:t.enabled)!==!1}},description:{short:K.shortDescription(B.msg({defaultMessage:"Which SSH engine carries Code sessions: the OpenSSH ssh program on the device, or the app\u2019s built-in SSH library. Unset or auto: the build\u2019s default.",id:"SshTransportHint"})),long:K.longDescription("`system-openssh`: the app makes every SSH connection by running an OpenSSH `ssh` program \u2014 the one `sshClientPath` names, otherwise the first `ssh` on the user's PATH (on Windows, a Win32-OpenSSH `ssh.exe`: the PATH one, else the in-box or Microsoft-installed client) \u2014 so the organization's own OpenSSH build, with its Kerberos/GSSAPI, certificate and `ssh_config` support, is what authenticates. The program must be OpenSSH 7.6 or newer (Windows: Win32-OpenSSH 9.4 or newer). When `sshClientPath` is set and that program cannot be used, sessions fail with an error telling the user to ask their IT administrator rather than falling back; when it is unset and Windows has no usable client, the built-in library is used.\n\n`builtin`: the app's built-in SSH library makes the connection, whatever the build's default.\n\n`auto` or unset: the build's default engine.\n\nAn explicit value applies to new connections (sessions already connected keep their engine) and overrides the build's default in both directions, including any remote switch-off Anthropic ships for the OpenSSH engine \u2014 so with `system-openssh` set, switching back is done here, by setting `builtin`.",{docsUrl:`${zn.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/ssh-remote-sessions`})}}),allowedRepositories:K.field(K.annotate((()=>{let e=(a)=>a.source==="github",t=(a)=>a.source==="git",n={label:B.msg({defaultMessage:"Source",id:"cc9hc4+0K4"}),optionLabels:{github:B.msg({defaultMessage:"GitHub",id:"SYEyDpPjNk"}),git:B.msg({defaultMessage:"Git URL",id:"TpLDdW3nvS"})},description:{short:K.shortDescription(B.msg({defaultMessage:"Where the repository lives: GitHub (set repo) or any other Git host (set url).",id:"CodeRepoSourceHint"}))},predicates:{required:()=>!0}},i={ref:K.subfield(Fu.marketplaceRef.transform((a,l)=>{if(a===void 0)return;let d=a.trim().replace(/^refs\/heads\//,"");if(!nj(d))return l.addIssue("Branch names can only use letters, numbers, and . _ / -"),Re.z.NEVER;return d}),{label:B.msg({defaultMessage:"Branch",id:"CodeRepoBranch"}),description:{short:K.shortDescription(B.msg({defaultMessage:"Branch a session starts from. Leave it out for the repository\u2019s default branch. The person starting a session may type another.",id:"CodeRepoBranchHint"}),{docsOnly:!1})}}),name:K.subfield(Re.z.string().trim().min(1).max(64).optional(),{label:B.msg({defaultMessage:"Name",id:"C