new conversation or task in Chat, Cowork and Code starts on the default model (the first `inferenceModels` entry), and the model and effort choices a person makes are no longer saved as their defaults. When unset or `false`, a person's last model and effort choice is remembered per tab, as before. Choices saved before the setting was turned on are kept and apply again if it is turned off.",{docsUrl:`${at.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/configuration#models`})}}),pricing:gt.z.object({enabled:ie.field(gt.z.boolean().optional(),{flatKey:"inferenceModelPricingEnabled",readers:["desktop","code"],support:{enabled:{scopes:["3p"],availableInVersion:"1.37937.0"},executionTarget:"desktop"},default:{displayOnly:!1},title:ae.msg({defaultMessage:"Show estimated cost",id:"dqCubkxbYK"}),category:"connection",group:at.MODELS_GROUP,order:1,description:{short:ie.shortDescription(ae.msg({defaultMessage:"Show an estimated cost on the Usage page at Anthropic list price; turn on to set a multiplier or per-model rates.",id:"O20EMso86S"})),long:ie.longDescription("Off unless set: the Usage page shows token counts only, since the app cannot know your negotiated provider rates. `true` turns on a USD estimate priced at Anthropic's published list price and is the only switch that does: `inferenceModelPricingMultiplier` and `inferenceModelPricing` refine the estimate while this is on and are ignored otherwise; turning this off hides them in the config editors without clearing them. Claude Code performs the calculation, so the same figures appear in its own cost reporting for Code sessions. Model IDs Claude Code cannot map to a Claude model (an opaque gateway alias, an inference-profile ARN it cannot resolve) are left out of the estimate until `inferenceModelPricing` gives them a rate. A machine-level Claude Code managed `modelPricing` (MDM / managed-settings.json / server-managed) takes precedence over all three keys.",{docsUrl:`${at.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/configuration#models`})}}),multiplier:ie.field(ie.a